Chapter: LinearPolyFreeze
  cites Foreword chapter Linear

 Regression guard for LinearOwnership stage 1: freeze must stay
 polymorphic now that LinearTy survives type resolution. The
 parameterize walk recurses through the wrapper (a under linear
 becomes a bound TypeVar), instantiation freshens it, and unify
 strips it - so one freeze serves Integer and Text in one program.
 The old seed passes this too (erasure made it trivially true);
 the guard exists so no later stage silently monomorphizes it.

Section: Definitions

  opening : Text =
   show (freeze 21) & " " & freeze "seven"

